=== PART 4b. THE THREE WAYS TO SPEND A ROW, PRICED AT THE SAME MISS ===
For a row missing by z sigma_obs, what does each formulation contribute?
  live      : -log(sigma sqrt(2 pi)) - z^2/2
  skipped   :  0                                  <- a FREE gain of the above
  inflated  : -log(sigma_eff sqrt(2 pi)) - (z sigma/sigma_eff)^2/2,
              sigma_eff^2 = sigma^2 + sigma_rep^2  <- CHARGED for, and bounded
The inflated row's best case over all sigma_eff is sigma_eff = |miss|, i.e.
-log(|miss| sqrt(2 pi)) - 1/2 -- so inflation can never buy the whole row.

