=== PART 5. PREDICTIONS SCORED ===
P1.  PASS     only the three ocean_grad_* streams jump; the rest is slope
     jumpers: ocean_grad_dic, ocean_grad_d13c, ocean_grad_alk | jump/drift = 85x and 60x (bar 20x)
P2.  PASS     the cliff IS the rows appearing (exact identity)
     residual: lo -6.42e-13, hi -2.44e-12 (bar 1e-06); entry cost -10.13 vs 16f's -10.07
P3.  PASS     no taper moves the argmax inside the band
     taper, 30 m ramp -> 32.0 m | taper, 15 m ramp -> 32.0 m | taper, 60 m ramp -> 32.0 m
P4.  *** FAIL *** inflation's gain is a LARGE fraction of the skip's
     skip gives 10.01, inflation's best case 2.14 = 21 % (predicted > 50 %)
     FAILED IN THE DIRECTION THAT STRENGTHENS INFLATION, and the reasoning
     behind the prediction was wrong rather than the bar. I expected z^2/2 to
     dominate each row's logL; it does not, because the misses are only ~1.8
     sigma (z^2/2 ~ 1.6) while -log(sigma sqrt(2 pi)) carries the bulk. So
     inflation caps the give-away at ~1/5 of the skip's, not ~4/5.
P5.  *** FAIL *** sigma_rep is not small compared with sigma_obs
     DIC sigma_rep/sigma_obs spans 0.04-0.87 over h_ml [32, 192]; d13C 0.01-1.11
     ALSO FAILED, and this is the one that reframes the band. The
     representation error the band exists to prevent NEVER EXCEEDS ~1 sigma
     anywhere in h_ml's prior support. A mismatch that modest is being
     enforced with a 10-log-unit switch.


=== PART 6. THE CLIFF IS NOT WHY h_ml LEAVES THE BAND ===
objective's argmax over h_ml        32.00 m       -3959.84
best IN-BAND h_ml                   85.01 m       -4196.28
the cliff at the band's floor                          -10.01

THE PULL IS 24x THE CLIFF: 236 log-units of h_ml preference against
10.0 log-units of discarded rows. Deleting the three rows entirely
moves the argmax from 32 m to 32 m -- i.e. NOT AT ALL.

So the rows are not what drives h_ml out of the band, and no formulation of
them can pull it back in. That is a measurement about which of 16f sec.5.5's
options addresses the blocker, and it says: option 1 is not a tie-breaker
between formulations, it is a HARD CONSTRAINT worth the number below.

COST OF BOUNDING h_ml TO [85, 120], at init parameters: 236 log-units.
AN UPPER BOUND, and the same caveat class as 16f sec.5.2g's pump margin:
beta_max, kz and k_w can reallocate some of it in a refit, which is exactly
what a refit is for. It is NOT a claim about the refit's answer.


